"1ea61a1d-0999-4137-844a-3180b26070c1","position":{"commit_sha":"08667d8c6d55ddf5ece63daee532dfe4fdf9a015","position":"1787348264982948001-1ea61a1d-0999-4137-844a-3180b26070c1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"8e815313a14ca0ba86b590cb066eb4cc0f9a110fa31d55889560acd80795b3a3","event_uuid":"f0d25cd0-ad01-4953-b7a8-12c03b844513","position":{"commit_sha":"4692d26ebf5e6ed7c737a9a8a4f66fa36a2ff114","position":"1787349926806700001-f0d25cd0-ad01-4953-b7a8-12c03b844513"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"51e785b5573308fabc3e628363a3a85f0252221a43142b057384848ce39bac81","event_uuid":"961209d4-be94-4967-98f4-340052b4a647","position":{"commit_sha":"b759a0b4dcccdff2cc8ea48df81798ffb4236bb5","position":"1787350419185928001-961209d4-be94-4967-98f4-340052b4a647"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d11b77fdafa5875aac37e35ad64bfc3c55ba8a492d9df0d88cda688de9228550","event_uuid":"f11630a7-f62f-4f37-a823-e4d44fb78fa5","position":{"commit_sha":"2f249a35631c5f7da736de50b61339f59b847b97","position":"1787350423403435001-f11630a7-f62f-4f37-a823-e4d44fb78fa5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"obsolete","close_reason":"Operator rejected the premise. F01 must contain no character restriction. The provenance grammar remains unchanged, so no parser or ADR change is authorized.","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OPERATOR RULING (2026-08-21, via orchestrator session d958f0b2): The F01 character-restriction policy (banning U+003B and U+2014 in ticket writing) is an OVERREACH — it implements a character restriction that was previously REJECTED, precisely because the fragility introduced by enforcing character restrictions in documentation outweighs any benefit of restricting. Consequence for this ticket: the proposed multiline provenance grammar + ADR 0061 amendment is NOT the sanctioned direction. The conflict resolves the other way: remove/withdraw the F01 character restriction; the provenance close-guard grammar (which requires those code points) stands unchanged. This lane belongs to the documentation-infra session — leaving the ticket open for that session to action the withdrawal against F01.","timestamp":1787349926806700001}],"created_at":1787348248732686001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1ea61a1d-0999-4137-844a-3180b26070c1","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"fe47-c480-3036-45fe"}],"description":"## Context\n\nF01 introduced a documentation policy that bans U+003B and U+2014 in ticket writing. The deterministic close guard requires both code points in every `[non-codebase]` provenance declaration. F01 cannot close while satisfying both contracts.\n\n## Current enforcement\n\nThe parser reads only the first indented `provenance` continuation. It splits fields only on U+003B and extracts the required justification only after U+2014. The close precheck promotes parser failures to blocking status before completion verification. No punctuation-compliant syntax is accepted.\n\n## Historical basis\n\nADR 0061 pins the single-line grammar and states that the deterministic layer does not block. Ticket binary-cobwebby-bittern later promoted the parser to blocking close behavior without an accepted ADR amendment. ADR 0101 changes the canonical acceptance criterion tag and states that ADR 0061 remains unaffected.\n\n## Proposed direction\n\nAdopt a backward-compatible multiline grammar.\n\n```text\nprovenance:\n  environment = <value>\n  principal = <value>\n  privilege_posture = <value>\n  instrument = <value>\n  justification = <text>\n```\n\nContinue accepting the legacy grammar for historical records. Update the parser, close diagnostic, author guidance, plan-review lint, and tests to emit and accept the multiline form. Preserve deterministic provenance completeness and anti-laundering enforcement. Record the contract change through an ADR that amends or supersedes the relevant part of ADR 0061.\n\n## Alternatives\n\nRestoring advisory or grandfathered close behavior would weaken the close defense added by binary-cobwebby-bittern. Rewriting command outcomes as repository facts would misclassify their evidence. Adding legacy declarations would violate the F01 policy. A forced close would bypass signed completion verification.\n\n## Decision status\n\nPending operator approval. Do not implement this ticket or write an ADR until approved.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"961209d4-be94-4967-98f4-340052b4a647","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["documentation","architecture","gates"],"ticket_id":"c2ec-10b0-4bd9-430d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Support punctuation-compliant measurement provenance","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["685ecd2d-54c2-4e56-97be-519fbc95b25e","1ea61a1d-0999-4137-844a-3180b26070c1","f0d25cd0-ad01-4953-b7a8-12c03b844513","961209d4-be94-4967-98f4-340052b4a647","f11630a7-f62f-4f37-a823-e4d44fb78fa5"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787354431643917001,"uuid":"8bfb45dd-db45-4830-9811-0e6a80d02264"}